From 9b61f20a6d0f1f4791b33dc410293b09a4b8165c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Howard Chang <howard.chang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 01:57:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] log-handler: Add secondary timestamped logging

Add an optional timestamped text log that improves the debugging
experience by allowing developers to easily inspect event
sequences using standard text tools.

Implement a sanitize_to_ascii_ansi() state machine to strip
escape sequences. When enabled via the log-timestamp
configuration, the system prepends each ASCII line with a
formatted timestamp and a seven-digit line count.

Change-Id: Iffe6c4e29642bbdb2bcb514e36fb5b3c76ba0767
Signed-off-by: Howard Chang <howard.chang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
---
 log-handler.c                |  81 +++----
 meson.build                  |   1 +
 test/meson.build             |  28 +++
 test/test-log-handler.c      | 128 ++++++++++
 test/test-text-log-handler.c | 179 ++++++++++++++
 text-log-handler.c           | 436 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 util.c                       |  35 ++-
 util.h                       |   7 +
 8 files changed, 843 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/test-log-handler.c
 create mode 100644 test/test-text-log-handler.c
 create mode 100644 text-log-handler.c

